Safety scope: one kernel-owned privileged BCS context, no user batch uAPI;
no semaphores/scheduler/preemption clients. All unused VM branches reach an
owned read-only scratch page. Render wake and idle are required before shared
cache policy; MCR selection uses actual fuse bits and restores its before-image
on every error prefix. Unknown unicast agents are refused. Source firmware-lock
exception for DOP readback is preserved. Only N305 Gen12.0 applicable branches
are included; KBL/DG2/fast-color/hold-switchout paths do not apply.
The source two-word WA tail is MI_ARB_CHECK then MI_NOOP, not two NOOPs.
RAM/VM/context/GGTT remain pinned until source stop/reset quiescence, including
possibly-landed ELSQ failures; ambiguous reset terminally retains them.
Host model copies are explicitly not physical GPU-output evidence.

The two new C shims add two conventional INVALID_MMIO_REG definitions at
threshold25 (none at40). Current GT inventory:3 code lines at25,1 at40;
combined display+GT:15 at25,3 at40. No fenced/comment/marker matches or exemptions.

